course: dictionary
lesson: 3964
title: Words for strong feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words tell you how strongly a character feels. Fury is very strong, wild anger, so a character in a fury may be angry enough to lose control. «The dog barked at the mouse in fury» shows the dog was not just cross, it was wild with anger.
explain: Fury can also describe force, not only feelings. «The fury of the storm tore the roof off the barn» means the storm was powerful and dangerous. Scientists and geographers use the word the same way when they describe the fury of the sea or a volcano.
explain: In the tale, a dog called Fury says to a mouse, «I'll be judge, I'll be jury». That means one side would decide everything, which is a very unfair trial. Look at the words around fury to work out its meaning, then check your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
fact: Fury means very strong, wild anger.
fact: «The fury of the storm» means the great power and danger of a storm, the sea or a volcano.
fact: The adjective is furious: «She was furious when she found the broken window.»
fact: In ancient Greek and Roman stories, the Furies were three goddesses of revenge.
fact: «Cur» means a bad-tempered dog, and «prosecute» means take someone to court.
exercise: «The dog barked at the mouse in fury.» What does in fury mean? | Feeling very sleepy and calm | Feeling very cold and wet | *Feeling very strong, wild anger | Feeling very proud of a new toy
exercise: «The fury of the storm tore the roof off the barn.» What does fury mean here? | A small shower of rain | *Great power and force | Soft, gentle breeze | A happy song
exercise: Which word is the adjective form of fury? | Fury | Furry | Furies | *Furious
test: In the tale, the dog says «I'll be judge, I'll be jury». What does this show? | *One side would decide everything, a very unfair trial | Friends sharing a happy picnic | A fair game of chess | A kind teacher giving out prizes
test: What does «cur» mean? | A brave knight | A small kitten | *A bad-tempered dog | A kind teacher
exam: In the tale, what does «prosecute» mean? | Find a lost toy in the grass | *Take someone to court | Feed someone a big meal | Give someone a gift
